[ ] Make the queue loop an orchestrator over work runs =sandbox-driver-split $DECIDED 2026-09-25: orchestration is policy and sits outside the run primitives. Today it is done by the human, or by an interactive agent reading run manifests; the queue loop becomes one more orchestrator, for unattended nights, that starts work runs, not part of the sandbox. Dependency direction: the sandbox runner knows git, podman and harnesses, never ClearHead; the loop, its prompt template and its completed, blocked or unfinished classification live on the ClearHead side and call the runner. The runner's manifest records exit, cost, closing message and commits, never actions. Do after sandbox-root-containerfile and alongside the review-run work. LEARNED from runs 20260925-183142 and 20260925-215528: the generic runner still records action identifiers and snapshots a ClearHead-specific agents/loop; move action lookup, queue policy, prompt, completion/blocked/unfinished classification, and plan-proposal materialization to the ClearHead driver. The sandbox should accept generic run kind, prompt/artifact paths, harness and limits, and emit only run/commit/transcript facts. Preserve Quadlet isolation and the host verification flow.$ !2 ^2026-09-25T15:32 #01a0dab3-2d95-7d53-a65e-cb88d090e1bd
[ ] Export sandbox telemetry with standard attributes =sandbox-telemetry $Sessions export OTLP to the NUC collector, which writes agent-logs, agent-metrics and agent-traces jsonl under ~/.local/state/otelcol. From a container, the collector answers on the tailscale address, not host.containers.internal. Attributes, standard only: service.name and service.version from the harness itself, host.name, deployment.environment.name sandbox or interactive, vcs.repository.name, vcs.ref.head.name, vcs.ref.head.revision, cicd.pipeline.name agent-sandbox, cicd.pipeline.run.id for the run and cicd.pipeline.task.run.id per session. No clearhead attributes: runs join to actions through commits. The driver also timestamps build and each session in the manifest. Write the convention, with this table and its reasons, to docs/telemetry.md; interactive harness configs adopt host.name and deployment.environment.name. Sequence after the run-kind/driver boundary and automatic reconciliation stabilize: export meaningful terminal outcomes and systemd resource events, rather than instrumenting the current mixed-policy launcher twice.$ !3 ^2026-09-25T15:32 #01a0dab3-2dd5-7753-9f1d-25c1a3aea18a
[ ] Query sandbox runs with duckdb =sandbox-benchmarks $A saved duckdb query file over ~/agent-runs manifests and the collector jsonl, answering: cost and time per outcome; build time against agent time; tool calls and gate runs per session; sandbox against interactive sessions. Questions first, no dashboard. Do after sandbox-telemetry.$ !3 ^2026-09-25T15:32 <01a0dab3-2dd5-7753-9f1d-25c1a3aea18a #01a0dab3-2df6-7862-8b3a-df005de98823
[ ] Add review runs and harness selection =sandbox-cross-vendor-review $DECIDED 2026-09-25 with the human: work and review are separate run kinds, never bundled; deciding which to run is orchestration, kept outside both. A work run takes an action or prompt and mounts its clone read-write; its output is commits and a closing message. A review run takes a finished run's branch, refs/agent/base to agent/id, mounts that clone read-only so report-without-fixing is enforced, and writes findings to its manifest; no commits. Every run picks its harness, claude or pi, through an adapter taking a prompt file and a transcript path and reporting result and cost; a review usually uses the other vendor. The work prompt drops its self-review step, and the runbook's review gate moves to between a work run and landing. pi: headless via pi -p --mode json, final answer from the last message_end event, cost summed from usage.cost; image pins pi 0.85.1; the sandbox's own ChatGPT/Codex login lives in the agent-pi volume, OpenRouter as fallback via the openrouter_token secret; the subscription quota is shared with interactive work. agent-run shares the host pi settings minus pi-background-tasks, remote-pi and pi-memory, and the host agents directory, read-only.  LESSONS 2026-09-25 from a manual pi work run and two pi reviews, for the adapter: pi exits 0 even when its session ends in error, so read the last assistant message_end stopReason; the final text is in message_end content; cost sums message_end usage.cost.total. Take the outcome from the action's real state in read actions, which includes completed actions; an action missing from it is not completed. Exclude pi-mcp-adapter too, or pi loads the repo's own .mcp.json. The adapter must harvest like agent-run: an unharvested manual run lost its commits to agent-land, now guarded. Codex once hit WebSocket 1011 and then an invalid-key error on retry; a rerun succeeded. LEARNED: independent patch-only no-tool reviews missed numeric systemd properties, a missing-anchor reminder, and launcher-interruption behavior; host smoke plus an actual read-only branch checkout caught these. Make review a first-class run kind with the finished branch mounted read-only and access to the action decision/specs, full diff and validation evidence. Emit a durable verdict and findings; do not mutate reviewed files, choose a different vendor from the worker, and require explicit reconciliation of blocking findings before landing.$ !2 ^2026-09-25T15:32 #01a0dab3-2e1a-79c2-a788-6901734ddadf
[ ] Extract the sandbox into its own repo =sandbox-extract $Decided 2026-09-25 after evaluate-agent-runners: we write our own. Do after sandbox-driver-split, once the runner, harness adapters, harvest and land contain no ClearHead reference; grep for it as the check. The ClearHead driver stays on the ClearHead side. Extraction surfaces the remaining platform assumptions: the agents directory mount, the host pi paths, agent branch naming, and harvest assuming submodules. Proof of done: a run, harvest and land on a second repo that has no .clearhead directory.$ !3 ^2026-09-25T16:13 <01a0dab3-2d95-7d53-a65e-cb88d090e1bd <01a0dab3-2e1a-79c2-a788-6901734ddadf #01a0dad8-d9ba-79f1-8a9f-b5b68c0e3b0a
[ ] Automatically reconcile detached Quadlet runs =sandbox-auto-reconcile $Follow-up to landed run 20260925-215528. On the host, terminating the foreground systemctl start --wait caller left the Quadlet active with Result=success and ExecMainCode=0. The landed launcher correctly preserves the active unit and manifest; scripts/agent-status flags RECONCILE after it stops and scripts/agent-reconcile <id> is safe, idempotent manual recovery. For unattended operation, make terminal reconciliation automatic without a shell polling supervisor: use a systemd-owned completion/reaper mechanism or another bounded durable trigger. Preserve Git-only output, run isolation, no automatic mutation retry, and the explicit manual command. Acceptance: interrupt the launcher during a bounded no-model unit; the unit continues; when it exits the manifest reaches the correct terminal outcome and unit file is cleaned without operator intervention. Prove success, failure, timeout, OOM and manual stop retain accurate status; record recovery evidence in the manifest. Do not conflate this with the separate interactive model-control-channel design. Sequence first for unattended safety: systemd can outlive the launcher, but terminal manifest cleanup must not depend on an operator remembering the manual command. Preserve agent-reconcile as recovery and test a killed launcher against a real bounded unit.$ !1 ^2026-09-25T22:40 #01a0dc3a-f71b-7f82-97be-829c00623a8e
[ ] Gate an integration candidate before advancing main =sandbox-premerge-gate $Observed 2026-09-25: scripts/agent-land merged clearhead-core and platform before scripts/validate-pinned discovered a spec-conformance fixture failure, leaving both local main branches advanced despite exit 1. Make landing preflight the candidate in an isolated clean integration checkout/worktree with correct pinned submodules and reproducible gate dependencies, then advance the real branches bottom-up only after review and the gate pass. On failure preserve candidate branches, manifest and evidence, without a partially landed main. Preserve existing harvest-before-delete guard and report exact repo/ref/merge state. Do not claim cross-repo atomicity if a later merge or push fails; provide explicit recovery. Tests: failing gate leaves each real main unchanged; passing gate lands correct submodule pins and cleanup; fresh-clone npm dependency preparation (including approved tree-sitter-cli installer) is explicit rather than hidden in the developer checkout.$ !1 ^2026-09-25T22:45 #01a0dc3f-7483-7122-ba65-a73ece66b115
[=] Define a read-only planner and proposal handoff =sandbox-planner-contract $NEEDS DECISION: who approves and applies planner-proposed ClearHead action/charter changes—the human, a deliberating council, or a bounded driver policy? A genuinely read-only planner cannot directly mutate .clearhead; have it inspect the action, charter, specs, code and prior run evidence, validate feasibility, and emit a structured proposal with candidate CLI mutations, acceptance checks, dependencies, unknowns and stop/ask points. A distinct authorized materializer applies accepted changes through the ClearHead CLI and commits them; proposals are evidence, not authority. Alternative: grant narrowly scoped .clearhead write access in an isolated clone, but then this is a writer role, not read-only. Keep this ClearHead-specific policy in the driver, while the sandbox only hosts a generic read-only run kind and artifact. Preserve human authority over consequential decisions and avoid making a planner the top-down dispatcher. Decide the approval boundary before implementing.$ !3 ^2026-09-25T22:45 #01a0dc3f-bb67-76d2-a4ad-920ae1f90b3a
[=] Design interruptible interactive agent sessions =sandbox-interactive-control $NEEDS DECISION: what authenticated local input/control channel may interrupt an active sandbox model session without weakening the Git-only code-output boundary? Quadlet attachment alone cannot add a turn to current headless pi -p/Claude -p sessions. Specify cancellation versus checkpoint/resume, transport (persistent RPC or PTY relay), audit of human interventions, unit/manifest identity, credential isolation, failure/reconnect behavior, and whether a controller may write only prompts or broader tools. Preserve resource caps and independent review. This is a separate mode from unattended one-turn work; do not change the active runner until the authority and security contract is approved.$ !3 ^2026-09-25T22:45 #01a0dc3f-bb8e-7192-8113-f2b84efa412e
[ ] Pilot a lower-cost worker model on decided work =sandbox-cheap-worker-pilot $After the planner proposal contract and first-class cross-vendor review run exist, pilot a cheaper worker route such as DeepSeek via the sandbox harness adapter on a few bounded, already-decided actions in isolated Quadlets. Strong planning and independent review are advisory gates, not automatic authority; no self-review. Keep the same spend, wall-time and commit/gate contracts. Compare cost and elapsed time per accepted landed action, retries, stop/NEEDS DECISION rate and reviewer effort against a stronger worker baseline; cheap tokens alone are not the success metric. Record model/provider per session and let the driver select roles by policy without hard-coding ClearHead or a model into the generic sandbox. Do not make the cheap model the default for broad multi-seam or high-risk tasks without evidence.$ !3 ^2026-09-25T22:46 <01a0dc3f-bb67-76d2-a4ad-920ae1f90b3a <01a0dab3-2e1a-79c2-a788-6901734ddadf #01a0dc3f-e6ce-7cd3-802a-473ab21aa73a
